Here's a paragraph with a margin note, as a self-contained HTML snippet:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
  body {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 3rem auto;
    padding: 0 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .block {
    position: relative;
  }
  .margin-note {
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(100% + 1.5rem);
    top: 0;
    width: 180px;
    font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    background: #fff8c5;
    border-left: 3px solid #e0a800;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
    color: #5a4500;
  }
  .margin-note strong {
    display: block;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="block">
    <p>
      The lighthouse at Cape Verrin had stood unattended for nearly forty years
      before the survey team arrived. Its lamp room was cracked and salt-glazed,
      and the spiral staircase groaned under every step, yet the foundations
      were sound. The team's lead engineer remarked that it seemed to have been
      built not to resist the sea, but to outwait it.
    </p>
    <aside class="margin-note">
      <strong>To do</strong>
      Verify the "forty years" figure against the harbor authority records, and
      consider cutting the engineer's quote if we can't attribute it.
    </aside>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
```

